From: edk2-cix <edk2-cix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:53:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Platform/CIX/Sky1: enable PCIe SMMU

The IORT mapped the PCIe root complex straight to the ITS, so the OS
saw no SMMU in front of PCIe devices.  Set PCIE_SMMU_ENABLE: the IORT
then describes the PCIe SMMUv3 (SMMU0_BASE, PCIe hub TCU interrupts)
and routes the root complex's IDs through it; MSIs still reach the ITS
through the SMMU node's ID mapping.  The PCIe PMCG stays out of the
IORT, since PMCG_ENABLE is 0.
---
 Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/AcpiSocTables/CommonDefines.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/AcpiSocTables/CommonDefines.h b/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/AcpiSocTables/CommonDefines.h
index 31fb399c..2cc571c4 100644
--- a/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/AcpiSocTables/CommonDefines.h
+++ b/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/AcpiSocTables/CommonDefines.h
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 #define RAMOOPS_RES_SIZE   0xa0000
 
 // IORT
-#define PCIE_SMMU_ENABLE        0
+#define PCIE_SMMU_ENABLE        1
 #define MM_HUB_SMMU_ENABLE      1
 #define SUB_SYSTEM_SMMU_ENABLE  0
 
